@startuml
title RAG Bot QA Flow with Gaps, Logging, Golden Set Tests and Evaluation

actor User as U
participant "Telegram Bot\n(bot_telegram.py)" as TG
participant "RAG Core\n(rag_core.py)" as RAG
participant "Embedding Model\n(BAAI/bge-m3)" as EMB
database "FAISS Index\n(faiss.index + meta.jsonl)" as FAISS
collections "KB Files\n(knowledge-base/*.txt)" as KB
participant "OpenAI LLM\n(chat.completions)" as LLM
collections "Logger\n(JSONL)" as LOG
actor "Test Runner\n(test_golden_set.py)" as TEST
collections "Golden Set\n(golden_set.jsonl)" as GS

== Prepare artificial gaps ==
note over KB
(Once) Editor removes 2–3 key entities
(e.g., 'VoidCore', 'Xarn Velgor', 'Synth Flux')
to simulate missing knowledge.
Then update_index.py rebuilds FAISS.
end note
RAG -> KB : scan & chunk files
RAG -> EMB : encode chunks
RAG -> FAISS : rebuild index (add vectors)

== Normal user request ==
U -> TG : 1) "User message(s)"
activate TG
TG -> RAG : 2) debounce + buffer -> generate_answer(query, history)
activate RAG

alt Guard: index missing or empty
  RAG -> FAISS : check existence/mtime
  FAISS --> RAG : not found / size==0
  RAG -> TG : "I don't know (index unavailable)"\n+ suggest retry
  TG -> LOG : write log{timestamp, query, found_chunks=0,\nanswer_len=short, success=false, sources=[] ,\nerror="IndexMissing"}
  deactivate RAG
  deactivate TG
  return
else Index OK
  RAG -> EMB : 3) embed_query(query)
  EMB --> RAG : q-vector
  RAG -> FAISS : 4) search top-k
  FAISS --> RAG : hits (chunks, scores, meta)

  alt No chunks retrieved
    RAG -> TG : "I don't know" (+ ask clarifying info)
    TG -> LOG : log{found_chunks=0, success=false, sources=[]}
    deactivate RAG
    deactivate TG
    return
  else Chunks found
    RAG -> RAG : 5) Sanitize context\n(strip injections, redact secrets, drop suspicious links)
    RAG -> LLM : 6) Build prompt (system+few-shot+history+contexts)\n-> call LLM
    activate LLM

    alt LLM error/timeout
      LLM --> RAG : error
      RAG -> TG : graceful error message
      TG -> LOG : log{found_chunks>0, success=false,\nerror="LLMTimeout"}
      deactivate LLM
      deactivate RAG
      deactivate TG
      return
    else OK
      LLM --> RAG : 7) Answer (reasoning summary + final)
      RAG -> TG : 8) Answer + sources footer
      TG -> LOG : 9) log{timestamp, query,\nfound_chunks=k, answer_len, success=heuristic,\nsources=[doc_path:chunk_idx...]}
    end
  end
end
deactivate RAG
deactivate TG

== Automated evaluation (Golden Set) ==
TEST -> GS : 1) load 10–15 Qs\n(8 positives, 3–5 negatives)
loop for each question
  TEST -> TG : 2) send question (simulated user)
  TG -> RAG : 3) generate_answer(...)
  RAG -> EMB : 4) embed + retrieve
  RAG -> FAISS : 5) search
  FAISS --> RAG : hits
  RAG -> LLM : 6) prompt with few-shot + contexts
  LLM --> RAG : 7) answer
  RAG -> TG : 8) answer + sources
  TG -> LOG : 9) log row (same schema)
  TEST -> TEST : 10) evaluate heuristic\n(e.g., contains expected keywords,\nanswer_len > min, not "I don't know" for positives,\nIS "I don't know" for negatives)
end

== Analytics over logs ==
participant "Analytics" as ANA
ANA -> LOG : Load logs (*.jsonl)
ANA -> ANA : Aggregate KPIs (может быть процент успешных по топикам, top queries, непокрытые процессы)
ANA -> KB : Produce backlog to expand/clean docs
ANA -> FAISS : (after KB updates) trigger rebuild

== Failure points legend ==
note over RAG,FAISS
Potential failures:
- Empty or missing FAISS index
- Invalid chunk meta (missing text/title)
- LLM timeout / rate limit
- Prompt-injection attempt in chunks
end note

@enduml
